riptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-13T16:59:38Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T16:59:56Z","body":"My latest commit appears to have fixed the problem (I'll squash it later) with error related to deferred method. From my tests it seems to be okay. Still, I'm not sure if I got it right, especially if that `if` at the beginning of `_set_main_scene_state()` could be safely removed or did it guard against some weird edge case apart from mismatch of `get_edited_scene()` due to stacking of multiple deferred calls.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2877303526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905655536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105502#issuecomment-2905655536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105502","id":2905655536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tMMjw","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-23T19:53:33Z","updated_at":"2025-05-23T19:53:33Z","body":"Maybe instead of adding a custom closing logic, you could reuse `_discard_changes()`?\r\n```C++\r\nbool EditorNode::close_scene() {\r\n\tcurrent_menu_option = SCENE_CLOSE;\r\n\t_discard_changes();\r\n}\r\n```\r\nShould do the same I think, but without requiring extra changes.\r\n\r\nYour current code does work on brief testing, but not sure if it doesn't break anything.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2905655536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906679238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105502#issuecomment-2906679238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105502","id":2906679238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tQGfG","user":{"login":"tehKaiN","id":16180344,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTgwMzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16180344?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN","html_url":"https://github.com/tehKaiN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T09:11:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T09:13:17Z","body":"Indeed it appears to work, but with some problems, making a step backwards:\r\n\r\n1. When running the test code with other scene opened beforehand, the message `ERROR: res://ed_script.gd:18 - Cannot call method 'close_scene' on a null value.` triggers sometimes. My proposed changes directly mitigate its causes. Sadly, I don't see a way of getting around it without refactoring the `call_deferred()` part.\r\n2. When running the test code without redundant `close_scene()` and having an opened scene beforehand, the last scene doesn't close. This requires further investigation if you choose that I should go further this way.\r\n\r\nStill, I'm not convinced that it's the best way to go. In my book, parts of code that are hard to understand are to be either simplified or documented, and it's quite apparent that the latter isn't that obvious for `call_deferred()` part which I've replaced. I know it's a risk that it could introduce regressions/unforeseen problems in other parts, though, but if it means antything, I can oblige myself to fixing them as they come.\r\n\r\nUltimately, it's your call, so let me know if I should try to further debug your proposed approach or should I keep my version and squash the commits.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906679238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916752647","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105502#issuecomment-2916752647","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105502","id":2916752647,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t2h0H","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T15:24:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T15:24:25Z","body":"Here's a complete `close_scene()` method:\r\n```C++\r\nbool EditorNode::close_scene() {\r\n\tint tab_index = editor_data.get_edited_scene();\r\n\tif (tab_index == 0 && get_edited_scene() == nullptr && editor_data.get_scene_path(tab_index).is_empty()) {\r\n\t\treturn false;\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\ttab_closing_idx = tab_index;\r\n\tcurrent_menu_option = SCENE_CLOSE;\r\n\t_discard_changes();\r\n\treturn true;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nTested and it works correctly in all cases (though I don't have your project to test your example). Also, unlike your method, it works with Reopen Closed Scene.\r\n\r\nRefactoring is fine, but this PR does not need it, so you can open a separate one for that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2916752647/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2917449892","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105502#issuecomment-2917449892","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105502","id":2917449892,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t5MCk","user":{"login":"tehKaiN","id":16180344,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTgwMzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16180344?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN","html_url":"https://github.com/tehKaiN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T19:53:17Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T19:53:17Z","body":"I've pushed your suggestions. It works, with the same problem I've encountered at the beginning of working on this PR. I've opened completely unrelated scene, opened the editor script from PR description and here's the log:\r\n\r\n```\r\nGodot Engine v4.5.dev.custom_build (c) 2007-present Juan Linietsky, Ariel Manzur & Godot Contributors.\r\n--- Debug adapter server started on port 6006 ---\r\n--- GDScript language server started on port 6005 ---\r\nOpening scene from res://test_1.tscn\r\nClosing scene, result: 0\r\nOpening scene from res://test_2.tscn\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe fix 